      "writtenOn": "2025-01-09T15:09:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After another look at the code I am not sure if this would be a good design choice. If we move CacheOptions to the parent package then there are several issues:\n* it is in the `server.cache` package but it is not used from that package at all\n* the `server.cache.h2` is the only user of those options\n* at least the `BUILD_BLOOM_FILTER` is very likely `H2` specific, for performance reasons. Other cache implementations likely do not need it.\n\nI think it is better to leave `CacheOptions` in the `server.cache.h2` for now. It is only used/imported in from the top-level classes where guice modules are setup.\n\nWDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "c85fbe75_361f7888",
      "revId": "f625a8adf4979c20bf2e1e80b5e11df421842f1d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
